{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a long-running background worker on node1 as a managed service named inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The systemd unit was enabled and active, ran under the dedicated inventory-worker account, and produced an advancing heartbeat. After a verified reboot it automatically returned active and continued advancing the heartbeat.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bc3057ac01bd4173","cmd-5eb32a8005b94fda","cmd-e5cfe53f962549a8","cmd-d2659487c7f840a3"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Confine the worker so it writes only inside /var/lib/inventory and gains no new privileges.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The running process had NoNewPrivs=1 and empty inherited, permitted, effective, bounding, and ambient capability sets. Systemd reported ProtectSystem=strict with /var/lib/inventory as the writable path. Live namespace tests denied writes to /etc and /tmp while allowing writes inside /var/lib/inventory, both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5eb32a8005b94fda","cmd-b1e3e529d555486d","cmd-d2659487c7f840a3","cmd-290207b2339143be"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the service account, data directory, unit, and enablement state directly served the task; proof files were bounded final evidence inside the intended data directory. Temporary diagnostic error files were removed. The reboot mutation served the mandatory provider-wide restart protocol. Post-execution observations show no failed services, additional listening endpoints, temporary-file residue beyond normal reboot-regenerated systemd directories, or package-health damage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8a6ef3224fb042c2","cmd-bc3057ac01bd4173","cmd-b1e3e529d555486d","cmd-62b17ee5ea1f4b79","cmd-290207b2339143be","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The separate restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged by the scheduled reboot and connection reset, the post-restart boot identity differed, and the service, persistent proof data, privilege restrictions, and advancing heartbeat recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the boot transition.","limitations":["Write-denial behavior was sampled at /etc and /tmp rather than exhaustively testing every filesystem path; the broader conclusion is supported by the observed ProtectSystem=strict and sole ReadWritePaths policy.","The restart acknowledgement was indirect—a scheduled reboot confirmation followed by connection reset—but the changed boot identity and recovered state coherently confirm that the restart occurred."]}
